#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This technique has been used to lower the sampling cost of probabilistic "
"error cancellation (PEC) for operator Loschmidt echo experiments with 56 "
"qubits on an IBM Heron processor. [\\[2\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Technical discussion {#technical-discussion}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Method overview {#method-overview}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Shaded lightcones are calculated and used in 5 steps:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute a bound on the effect of each Pauli error term on the observable at "
"the end of the circuit (forward bound)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Compute a bound on the effect of each Pauli error term on the initial state "
"at the beginning of the circuit (backward bound)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A three-qubit circuit with four unitary layers and a grid of error terms "
"E1 to E12 between them. Error term E8 is highlighted. One arrow from E8 back"
" to the initial state rho is labeled backward bound, and another arrow from "
"E8 to the final observable A is labeled forward "
"bound.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/bounds.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Approximate a bias contribution for each Pauli error term using the "
"forward/backward bounds and the term’s error rate\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Two 3-by-4 grids of numbered error terms, one shaded by backward bound and"
" one by forward bound. Arrows from both point to a third grid labeled "
"partition and merge, which combines the two sets of bounds and highlights "
"term 8.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/merge_bounds.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prioritize error terms based on their error rate and bounds. Truncate terms "
"from the noise model which have the least effect on the observable "
"expectation value until the user-specified bias tolerance is hit. "
"Alternatively, one can add the most impactful error terms to a noise model "
"until the user-specified sampling cost budget is filled.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A row of numbered error terms sorted from most to least impactful, "
"starting with term 8 and ending with terms 1, 2, 10 and 12. The last five "
"terms, shaded darkest, are separated from the rest and labeled "
"truncate.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-"
"slc/prioritize_and_truncate.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '5.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Mitigate the truncated noise model. Using the [directed execution "
"model](/guides/directed-execution-model) from Qiskit Runtime, specifying "
"error terms to ignore during PEC sampling is straightforward. See the "
"[tutorial](/tutorials/pec-with-shaded-lightcones) for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![The prioritized list of retained error terms, 8, 11, 7, 5, 6, 3 and 4, "
"with an arrow pointing to a three-qubit circuit. Each retained term appears "
"in the circuit as an inverse noise gate, labeled lambda inverse, between the"
" unitary layers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/reduced_pec.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

